 "about": "Wave 4 real items (MADE industrial/digital and SUB). share = relative customers, rel = relative price (normalised on install so share x rel adds up to 1, the going ticket does not move). mat = inputs (bill of materials, feed, platform) and dir = other direct cost, both as shares of the item's price; scaled on install so the weighted cost of the menu equals the trade's cost-of-sales share (not for salmon, whose books carry the cohort cost). m: made (stocked batches), proj (made to order, bid or fixed-price project), svc, sub (period weeks, churn per period). min = labour minutes per unit, scrap = share of units scrapped (cost is grossed up), lead = days, batch = units per production run, minQty = minimum order, hours = scope of a bid in hours, over = overrun risk, dev = hours to develop a digital title, half = weeks for weekly sales to halve, yield = tonnes of product per tonne of fish. inputs = [name, share of the input cost].",
